.TH TRACEROUTE 1
.SH NAME
traceroute \- the routers on the way to a host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B traceroute
.I host
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B traceroute
sends pings with a growing time to live, 1 to 30: each router on the way
answers "time exceeded", and its address and the time are printed, one
line per hop
.RB ( *
when nothing answered within 2 seconds). It stops when
.I host
itself answers.
.PP
.B traceroute
is another name of
.BR fetch (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the host was reached within 30 hops, 1 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (1),
.BR fetch (1)
.SH BUGS
QEMU's user network does not count the time to live, so every host is one
hop away there; the answers of real routers are untested.
